``break-in-finally`` and ``continue-in-finally`` are now emitted when the
statement is nested inside the ``finally`` clause, for example under an ``if``
or ``with``, or in the ``finally`` of a ``try``/``except*``, matching the
``SyntaxWarning`` raised by Python 3.14. ``not-in-loop`` is now emitted for a
``break`` or ``continue`` nested inside a loop's ``else`` clause.

Refs #11621
